---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 13, 2026';
const contactEmail = 'contact@prettyprettyprettygood.org';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | prettyprettyprettygood"
  description="What prettyprettyprettygood collects through the contact form, why, and who it's shared with."
>
  <section class="section privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <div class="container privacy__inner">
      <div class="section-header privacy__header" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">privacy policy</p>
        <h1 id="privacy-heading">Short version: I collect what the contact form needs, and nothing else.</h1>
        <p class="section-lead">Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="privacy__prose" data-reveal>
        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          This site doesn't use tracking cookies, analytics, or advertising
          scripts. The only personal information collected is what you
          submit through the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>: your name,
          email address, website/domain, project message, and funding
          preference.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's used</h2>
        <p>
          Contact form submissions are sent directly to me by email so I can
          respond to your project inquiry. That's the only reason this
          information is collected — it isn't used for marketing, sold, or
          shared with anyone outside the services below.
        </p>

        <h2>Who it passes through</h2>
        <p>A few third-party services help the contact form work and keep it free of spam:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong> — receives your form submission and delivers it to me by email.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> — verifies you're a human, not a bot, before the form submits.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each of these services processes data on my behalf under their own
          privacy and security terms. None of them are used to advertise to
          you or to track you across other sites.
        </p>

        <h2>Ko-fi and PayPal</h2>
        <p>
          The Ko-fi and PayPal buttons on this site are plain links that take
          you to those companies' own websites. Nothing from those services
          is embedded on this site or shares data with it — anything you do
          on Ko-fi or PayPal is covered by their own privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site sets no tracking or advertising cookies. A small
          amount of information (like your theme preference) may be saved
          locally in your browser so the site remembers your choice — it
          never leaves your device.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          If you want to know what information I have about you, or want it
          deleted, email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy__inner {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .privacy__header {
    max-width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    margin-inline: 0;
  }

  .privacy__prose {
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .privacy__prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  .privacy__prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .privacy__prose p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .privacy__prose ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .privacy__prose li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .privacy__prose a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .privacy__prose a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary-dark);
  }
</style>
